{
  "id": "sdf-mesh-motion",
  "title": "A mesh moved across the beam's tiles leaves background records where it was and resolves where it went",
  "binding": "The positive leg boots an offscreen 256x144 world with a block on the left and, in the centre, a static placement of a prototype whose inline mesh is a quad and whose only shape is out of view. It selects the visibility debug view, which colors each pixel by the kind of its visibility record, captures a frame, moves the quad to the right with a row edit, across several of the beam's 16-pixel tiles, and captures again; then it pans the camera to the left with a camera row edit, so the whole scene crosses the tiles the other way, and captures a third time. Each region's kind is the analytic oracle's (SdfMeshCanaryOracleLawTests), with every row edit applied to the document it reads for the captures after it. The quad reads as mesh where it starts, the pixels it left read as background, and it reads as mesh where it went; after the pan the quad reads as mesh further right, the block reads as SDF where the pan took it, and the quad's old pixels read as background. The discriminating leg never moves the quad or the camera, so the vacated, moved and panned observations turn red.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": ["vulkan", "directx"],
  "requirements": ["gpu"],
  "timeoutSeconds": 60,
